INT. FONTAINE & BOATENG - BREAK ROOM - MORNING

A vending machine hums. A fruit bowl holds three plastic lemons. A whiteboard says "CULTURE IS KING" under a doodle of a crown with a frown.

MARGUERITE FONTAINE, 50s, the managing partner, in a cream suit, pours tea from a silver pot nobody else is allowed to touch. KWAME BOATENG, 40s, the other partner, in shirtsleeves, leans on the fridge. SLOANE RIDGEWAY, 30s, head of People & Culture, in athleisure, holds an iPad up like a shield. PHIL LINDQVIST, 50s, the accountant, sorts sweetener packets by color. In the doorway, an INTERN, 20s, holds a tray of pastries and wears a lanyard that says "INTERN."

MARGUERITE
Lovely morning.

KWAME
Lovely.

SLOANE
Lovely! We're so aligned.

PHIL
(to himself)
Pink, yellow, blue.

INTERN
I brought croissants.

MARGUERITE
Of course you did. You're our little sunbeam.

The Intern sets down the tray. Everyone takes one. Everyone chews. A long, pleasant silence.

KWAME
Marguerite and I wanted to thank you all for your hard work.

SLOANE
Amazing work.

PHIL
Sweetener's low.

MARGUERITE
Phil, your numbers this quarter are impeccable.

PHIL
Are they?

MARGUERITE
Impeccable. Isn't that the word, Kwame?

KWAME
It is.

The Intern smiles wider. Sloane taps her iPad.

SLOANE
So, as part of our culture refresh, we'll be transitioning a few roles.

PHIL
Which roles?

KWAME
Phil.

PHIL
Which?

MARGUERITE
Yours, dear.

Phil sets down the packets. The Intern's smile slips.

INTERN
I'm sorry, did you say transition?

SLOANE
Offboarding, practically speaking.

INTERN
(softly)
Mine too?

MARGUERITE
Not at all. You'll be taking Phil's desk.

INTERN
I'm sorry. What's my name?

KWAME
Pardon?

INTERN
You've called me intern for six months. I told you my name on day one.

MARGUERITE
Did you? I'm sure it was lovely.

INTERN
It's Dewey.

DEWEY
(CONT'D)
Dewey Park. I'm the one who built your billing system.

Silence. The fridge clicks. Phil, still holding a pink packet, looks at Dewey for the first time.

PHIL
He did.

KWAME
We know.

DEWEY
Then you know the system doesn't run without me.

MARGUERITE
We have a plan for that.

DEWEY
Do you.

He takes off the lanyard. Sets it on the tray.

DEWEY (CONT'D)
Then enjoy the croissants.
